==English==
{{wikipedia|borscht}}
[[Image:Borscht.jpg|thumb|borscht]]

===Etymology===
1884 or 1808. {{etyl|yi|en}} {{term|באָרשט|tr=borsht|sc=Hebr|lang=yi}}, from {{etyl|ru|en}} or {{etyl|uk|en}} {{term|борщ|tr=boršč|lang=uk}}.

===Alternative forms===
* [[borsch]], [[borshch]], [[borsht]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/bɔrʃt/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɔː(r)ʃt|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[beetroot]]/[[beet]] [[soup]] that can be [[serve]]d hot or cold, usually with [[sour cream]].

====Derived terms====
* [[cheap like borscht]]
* [[Borscht Belt]]

